---
source: tests/cli/tools.rs
info:
  program: slcr
  args:
    - tools
    - add
    - "--help"
  env:
    XDG_DATA_HOME: "[DATA_HOME]"
---
success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Declare a tool in SLCR.toml: fetch its descriptor, check it, pin it, and install it

Usage: slcr tools add [OPTIONS] <SOURCE>

Arguments:
  <SOURCE>
          Where to fetch the descriptor from: an `https://` URL, or the path to a file inside the project

Options:
      --as <NAME>
          The name to declare the tool under, which validators refer to it by. Defaults to the descriptor's own name

      --enable-colors <ENABLE_COLORS>
          Whether to color the output

          Possible values:
          - always: Always color the output
          - never:  Never color the output
          - auto:   Detect whether the terminal is a tty before deciding to color
          
          [default: auto]

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Sets the maximum log level. Defaults to INFO. Options are 'trace', 'debug', 'info', 'warn', 'error', and 'off'. 'off' implies no logger will occur. Options are case-insensitive
          
          [env: LOG_LEVEL=]
          [default: info]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

----- stderr -----
